######################################################################
### PARLEY - THE PEOPLE PANELS   (integration contract v1, item 19)
###
### A types-only file. NO registration in gui/scripted_widgets is needed, and
### adding one would be wrong: only a WINDOW is registered there (see the
### header of gui/tnt_diplomacy_window.gui). Same standing as gui/tnt_types.gui,
### gui/tnt_panels.gui, gui/tnt_panel_multiselect.gui and
### gui/tnt_panel_contract.gui, none of which is registered either.
###
### WHAT IS IN HERE
###   1. HOSTAGES   overlay index 16, sides 0 and 1 - two tnt_picker_panel
###                 derivatives over tnt_list_hostage_p / _r.
###   2. WARD       *** RETIRED V16, USER ITEM 5 *** - the two derivatives are
###                 commented out and overlay index 17 is DORMANT. Was: sides 0
###                 and 1 over tnt_list_ward_p / _r.
###   3. COURTIERS  overlay 18, both sides - tnt_panel_multi over
###                 tnt_list_courtier_* (available) / tnt_sel_courtier_* (chosen).
###   4. SUBJECTS   overlay 19, both sides (V26) - tnt_panel_multi over tnt_list_subject_* / tnt_sel_subject_*.
### GRANT INDEPENDENCE HAS NO PANEL AND NO OVERLAY INDEX, by the contract: it
### is a bool pair, and the fealty row already proves a bool needs only
### tnt_item_row_toggle plus a tnt_show_ gate. Nothing about it is in this file.
###
### THE INDICES ARE THE CONTRACT'S, NOT THIS FILE'S CHOICE. 16 / 17 / 18 are
### allocated in section 3 of the integration contract; 14 and 15 were left
### alone although technically free, because the frozen table still names them
### as the PIETY and INFLUENCE row identities and that table is quoted from four
### files. Overlay 13 is now RETIRED with the captive picker (user item 7), and
### side 1 of it - once RESERVED for the partner-side captive panel - is released
### with it. Neither half is reused. Indices 8 and 11 are likewise RETIRED, not
### free, with the prisoner terms and the third-party non-aggression promise.
### V13 USER ITEM 1 ADDS THREE MORE: 3 (alliance), 4 (truce) and 7 (the granted
### claim - both overlay sides, and the row index too). A DESIGN REFUSAL, not a
### bug fix: all three let a player buy at this table what vanilla deliberately
### gates behind a lifestyle investment - the two pacts behind the Diplomacy perk
### defensive_negotiations_perk
### (GAME\common\character_interactions\00_alliance.txt:1184,
### GAME\common\scripted_triggers\03_fp2_scripted_triggers.txt:732), the claim
### behind Learning and a Court Chaplain's council task
### (GAME\common\council_tasks\00_court_chaplain_tasks.txt:1088). NEVER reused,
### NEVER renumbered.
### V16 USER ITEM 5 ADDS ONE MORE: 17 (the ward / fosterage picker), retired
### because the term was too abusable on points and the hostage picker in section 1
### covers the same immersive ground.
### The frozen table now reads: in use 5, 6, 10, 12, 16, 18, 19 (V26); free 1,
### 9, 14, 15, 20+; RETIRED, not free 2, 3, 4, 7, 8, 11, 13, 17.
###
### WHY DERIVED TYPES RATHER THAN SIX BODIES OF BLOCKOVERRIDES IN THE WINDOW.
### That is the shipped pattern and the reason is recorded at
### gui/tnt_panel_multiselect.gui section 5: an instantiation written from a
### naming contract alone gets block bodies wrong across an agent boundary, so
### the panel author ships working defaults and the window instantiates with one
### line. These six are that same deal - each carries its own `visible`, its own
### title, its own lists and its own setters.
###
### CROSS-FILE DERIVATION IS PROVEN IN THIS MOD, and load order does not matter:
### gui/tnt_panel_contract.gui loads BEFORE gui/tnt_panels.gui alphabetically and
### still derives `type tnt_panel_contract = tnt_editor_panel` and
### `type tnt_contract_right_row = tnt_toggle_line` from it. tnt_picker_panel
### lives in gui/tnt_types.gui and tnt_panel_multi / tnt_multi_row_char in
### gui/tnt_panel_multiselect.gui; both are resolved the same way.
###
### R-LAYOUT (this project's own law, one debugging session each):
###   * no `position` / `parentanchor` on a direct child of hbox / vbox /
###     flowcontainer - the rule row texts below are plain expanding children
###     and carry neither;
###   * every decorative widget carries alwaystransparent = yes, because a
###     non-transparent sibling over a button kills the click AND the hover;
###   * every text that prints GAME text is autoresize = no with the inherited
###     elide (the rule lines are the documented exception - they print OUR loc
###     and use the text_multi + max_width recipe the non-aggression panels
###     shipped, before user item 1 retired them; the recipe is unchanged);
###   * every datamodel item carries a FIXED size (PDX: "required for
###     performance reasons", GAME\gui\window_epidemics.gui:449-450).
###   * NO GetScriptedGui in any `visible` or `down` (Law R11). Every test below
###     is a variable read or a datamodel emptiness test.
###
### THE PANELS' OWN `parentanchor = center` is inherited from the two base types
### and stays legal: their parent is tnt_picker_overlay, a plain widget, which
### arranges nothing.
###
### IDENTIFIERS USED HERE THAT THIS FILE DOES NOT OWN (all from the contract's
### register, section 1.B): the variables tnt_hostage_p/_r,
### the lists tnt_list_hostage_p/_r, tnt_list_courtier_p/_r,
### the selections tnt_sel_courtier_p/_r, the scripted guis
### tnt_pick_hostage_<side>_open/_set/_clear
### and tnt_sel_courtier_<side>_add/_remove/_clear, and the two prices
### tnt_val_courtier_multi_p_value / _r_value.
### RETIRED V16, USER ITEM 5 - this file no longer names tnt_ward_p/_r,
### tnt_list_ward_p/_r or tnt_pick_ward_<side>_open/_set/_clear on any live line;
### all of them are gone from their owning files too.
###
### ONE NAME IS NOT IN THE REGISTER AND IS FLAGGED IN THE BUILD REPORT:
### tnt_multi_courtier_p_open / tnt_multi_courtier_r_open, the panel OPENERS for
### the two courtier panels. The contract lists courtier's add / remove / clear
### but no opener. The name follows the only shipped precedent -
### tnt_multi_<item>_<side>_open (tnt_multi_title_p_open, and
### tnt_multi_prisoner_p_open until user item 7 retired it - the precedent it set
### stands) - and the distinction is load-bearing rather than
### cosmetic: the tnt_multi_* opener runs the PRUNE after the fill, so the
### already-chosen courtiers leave the available column. The tnt_pick_* form
### would show every candidate in both columns at once, and in a two-list panel
### a row's column IS its selection state.
######################################################################

types TwdPeople
{

	####################################################################
	### 1. HOSTAGES - overlay index 16
	###
	### ONE hostage per side, so this is a single-object picker and not a
	### multi-select: tnt_hostage_p is a character VARIABLE, and the row's
	### filled state is that character's own head (tnt_chosen_char).
	###
	### THE RULE LINE IS NOT DECORATION. The non-aggression panels gained one
	### because "the old picker never said who qualified and nobody could tell
	### what the list meant", and a hostage list is the worst case of that: the
	### candidates come from tnt_hostage_candidate_trigger and a player looking
	### at four of his children has no way to know why the fifth is missing.
	### Same text_multi recipe as those panels.
	###
	### `down` is answerable here and IS answered, unlike in the multi-select
	### panels: with one slot, "is this the chosen one" is ObjectsEqual against
	### the stored variable - the shipped tnt_picker_row_char default.
	####################################################################

	### 16 / side 0 - the hostage the PLAYER sends.
	type tnt_panel_hostage_p = tnt_picker_panel
	{
		name = "tnt_panel_hostage_p"
		visible = "[And( EqualTo_CFixedPoint( TntNum('tnt_picker'), '(CFixedPoint)16' ), EqualTo_CFixedPoint( TntNum('tnt_picker_side'), '(CFixedPoint)0' ) )]"

		blockoverride "tnt_picker_panel_title" { text = "tnt_picker_title_hostage_p" }

		blockoverride "tnt_picker_panel_empty"
		{
			text = "tnt_picker_empty"
			visible = "[IsDataModelEmpty( TntList('tnt_list_hostage_p') )]"
		}

		blockoverride "tnt_picker_panel_list"
		{
			vbox = {
				name = "tnt_rows_hostage_p_outer"
				layoutpolicy_horizontal = expanding
				spacing = 6

				text_multi = {
					name = "tnt_rule_hostage_p"
					layoutpolicy_horizontal = expanding
					text = "tnt_picker_rule_hostage"
					autoresize = yes
					max_width = 430
					default_format = "#weak"
					alwaystransparent = yes
					fontsize_min = 12
					using = Font_Size_Small
				}

				vbox = {
					name = "tnt_rows_hostage_p"
					layoutpolicy_horizontal = expanding
					spacing = 3
					datamodel = "[TntList('tnt_list_hostage_p')]"

					item = {
						tnt_picker_row_char = {
							datacontext = "[Scope.Char]"
							size = { 0 45 }

							blockoverride "tnt_row_onclick" { onclick = "[TntPickChar('tnt_pick_hostage_p_set')]" }
							blockoverride "tnt_row_down"    { down = "[ObjectsEqual( TntVar('tnt_hostage_p').Char, Character.Self )]" }
						}
					}
				}
			}
		}
	}


	### 16 / side 1 - the hostage the PARTNER sends. Same panel, his list.
	type tnt_panel_hostage_r = tnt_picker_panel
	{
		name = "tnt_panel_hostage_r"
		visible = "[And( EqualTo_CFixedPoint( TntNum('tnt_picker'), '(CFixedPoint)16' ), EqualTo_CFixedPoint( TntNum('tnt_picker_side'), '(CFixedPoint)1' ) )]"

		blockoverride "tnt_picker_panel_title" { text = "tnt_picker_title_hostage_r" }

		blockoverride "tnt_picker_panel_empty"
		{
			text = "tnt_picker_empty"
			visible = "[IsDataModelEmpty( TntList('tnt_list_hostage_r') )]"
		}

		blockoverride "tnt_picker_panel_list"
		{
			vbox = {
				name = "tnt_rows_hostage_r_outer"
				layoutpolicy_horizontal = expanding
				spacing = 6

				text_multi = {
					name = "tnt_rule_hostage_r"
					layoutpolicy_horizontal = expanding
					text = "tnt_picker_rule_hostage"
					autoresize = yes
					max_width = 430
					default_format = "#weak"
					alwaystransparent = yes
					fontsize_min = 12
					using = Font_Size_Small
				}

				vbox = {
					name = "tnt_rows_hostage_r"
					layoutpolicy_horizontal = expanding
					spacing = 3
					datamodel = "[TntList('tnt_list_hostage_r')]"

					item = {
						tnt_picker_row_char = {
							datacontext = "[Scope.Char]"
							size = { 0 45 }

							blockoverride "tnt_row_onclick" { onclick = "[TntPickChar('tnt_pick_hostage_r_set')]" }
							blockoverride "tnt_row_down"    { down = "[ObjectsEqual( TntVar('tnt_hostage_r').Char, Character.Self )]" }
						}
					}
				}
			}
		}
	}


	####################################################################
	### 2. WARD / FOSTERAGE - *** RETIRED V16, USER ITEM 5 ***
	###
	### Both picker panels below are commented out. ATOMIC PAIR with their two
	### instantiations at gui/tnt_diplomacy_window.gui:3240-3246: an instantiation
	### of a type that is not declared is a .gui LOAD error, so the declarations
	### and the instantiations went in one edit. Precedent for the pairing: the
	### retired claim panels, declarations commented at
	### gui/tnt_panel_multiselect.gui:1274 and :1355, instantiations at
	### gui/tnt_diplomacy_window.gui:2930, :2969.
	###
	### REASON (user item 5): the term was too abusable on points, and the hostage
	### term - section 1 above - already covers the same immersive ground. The
	### audit found the abuse STRUCTURAL rather than a single number; the full WARD
	### TOMBSTONE is in common/scripted_effects/tnt_32_apply.txt.
	###
	### OVERLAY INDEX 17 IS NOW DORMANT and must not be reassigned - the two
	### `tnt_picker` == 17 tests below were its only readers. Index 8 from the
	### retired prisoner picker was left dormant the same way
	### (common/scripted_guis/tnt_21_pickers.txt:304).
	###
	### The shared types these panels derived from - tnt_picker_panel and
	### tnt_picker_row_char in gui/tnt_types.gui - STAY LIVE: sections 1 and 3
	### still use them.
	####################################################################
#	####################################################################
#	### 2. WARD / FOSTERAGE - overlay index 17
#	###
#	### ONE child per side, and NO guardian sub-picker: the contract fixes the
#	### partner ruler as the guardian, so there is exactly one thing to choose
#	### and this is the same single-object shape as the hostage panels above.
#	###
#	### `_p` MEANS THE PLAYER'S CHILD GOES TO THE PARTNER'S COURT. That reading
#	### is fixed by the contract and may not be inverted here - the panel title
#	### keys are per-side for exactly that reason, because "choose a ward" with
#	### no owner named is the one sentence that could quietly swap them.
#	####################################################################
#
